A new, FREE monster among AI coding agents has been released — JCode

Developers claim that it runs 245 times faster than Claude Code and can handle up to 100 sessions simultaneously.

What it can do:
• One session only takes up 28 MB of RAM;
• It can assemble a whole team of AI agents — they will divide tasks among themselves, code collaboratively, and check each other's work;
• There is shared memory among all sessions, so context and changes are not lost;
• Supports APIs from Claude, OpenAI/ChatGPT/Codex, Gemini, GitHub Copilot, Azure, Alibaba Coding Plan, and other services;
• Works with local models through Ollama and LM Studio;
• Can edit, correct, restart, and debug code, gradually achieving the desired project outcome;
• Allows importing sessions from Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Cursor;
• Automatically generates codebase diagrams to quickly understand the project's structure.

